Keep a shared words as an empty list of text.
Place "tars" into words.
Place "rats" into words.
Place "arts" into words.
Place "star" into words.
Keep a shared graph as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared seen as an empty list of whole numbers.
Keep a shared firstword as empty text.
Keep a shared secondword as empty text.
Keep a shared differences as 0.
Keep a shared leftspot as 0.
Keep a shared rightspot as 0.
Keep a shared alike as 0.
For every place from 0 to 15.
Place 0 into graph.
For every place from 0 to 3.
Place 0 into seen.

To finish.
Set alike to 0.
If differences is 0, set alike to 1, return.
If differences is not 2, return.
The firstleft is the slice of firstword from leftspot to leftspot plus 1.
The firstright is the slice of firstword from rightspot to rightspot plus 1.
The secondleft is the slice of secondword from leftspot to leftspot plus 1.
The secondright is the slice of secondword from rightspot to rightspot plus 1.
If firstleft matches secondright.
If firstright matches secondleft, set alike to 1.

To scan from spot (a whole number).
If spot is more than the last position of firstword, Finish, return.
The one is the slice of firstword from spot to spot plus 1.
The two is the slice of secondword from spot to spot plus 1.
If one does not match two, add 1 to differences, set rightspot to leftspot, set leftspot to spot.
Scan from spot plus 1.

To check from first (a whole number) with second (a whole number).
Set alike to 0.
Set firstword to item first of words.
Set secondword to item second of words.
Set differences to 0.
Set leftspot to -1.
Set rightspot to -1.
If firstword matches secondword, set alike to 1, return.
Scan from 0.

To visit from node (a whole number).
If item node of seen is 1, return.
Set item node of seen to 1.
For every other from 0 to 3.
If item (node times 4 plus other) of graph is 1 and item other of seen is 0, Visit from other.

For every pair from 0 to 15.
The first is pair divided by 4.
The second is pair modulo 4.
If first is less than second.
Check from first with second.
If alike is 1, set item (first times 4 plus second) of graph to 1.
If alike is 1, set item (second times 4 plus first) of graph to 1.

The groups is 0.
For every start from 0 to 3.
If item start of seen is 0, add 1 to groups.
If item start of seen is 0, Visit from start.

Show groups.
